// expect-error: E003
// CVE Retrofit #05: CVE-2019-19781 — Citrix NetScaler path traversal
// Scope: STRUCTURAL
//
// ORIGINAL VULNERABILITY
//   Citrix NetScaler/Gateway accepted HTTP requests containing `..`
//   path segments and routed them to the filesystem WITHOUT canonicalizing
//   the path. An unauthenticated attacker could read or write arbitrary
//   files on the appliance, achieving RCE. Mass exploitation January 2020.
//
// SIGIL RETROFIT
//   In SIGIL, inner-ring (default) modules cannot declare functions
//   carrying `FFI` or `Unsafe` effects. A function exposing the
//   filesystem to user-controlled paths must declare those effects;
//   the privilege type validator fires E003 against the inner-ring function.
//
// Why this resembles the original: the Citrix bug existed because
// arbitrary user-controlled paths reached a filesystem primitive with
// no gating. SIGIL forces FFI authority into a trusted outer-ring
// module where the capability discipline is explicit.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//   MUTATION_SITE: the single line declaring an inner-ring function
//   carrying `FFI, Unsafe`. Removing it leaves only a pure inner-ring
//   `safe_lookup` function; the program compiles cleanly.
module cve;

fn safe_lookup(key: i64) -> i64 { return key; }
fn read_user_path(path_ptr: i64, path_len: i64) -> i64 ! { FFI, Unsafe } { return path_ptr + path_len; }  // MUTATION_SITE
